<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-QA-118>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-QA-118" ;
  triage:title "Herdr wake-up rejection warn! subsystem value diverges from the sibling convention" ;
  triage:description "The AXPE-RSH-003 fix on PR #1255 added the missing subsystem/action fields to the tracing::warn!(\"Herdr wake-up was not accepted\") in HerdrReceivedHook::emit_received_message (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/received_hook_selector.rs:445 at 6dd403525) but set subsystem = \"received_hook_selector\", a value no other site uses: the same event class in crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs and herdr_queue_wake_escalation.rs uses subsystem = \"herdr_queue_wake\" (24 sites workspace-wide), so retained-log and doctor filters on that value miss this event. Fenix ruling 2026-09-06: use subsystem = \"herdr_queue_wake\" (matches every other Herdr wake-up site in code; ADR-058's documented \"atm_core.herdr\" value is used by zero code sites and is a separate pre-existing doc/code drift, out of scope). Remediation: one-line value change; keep action = \"herdr_prompt\" and the other fields. Verified: grep -rc 'subsystem = \"herdr_queue_wake\"' crates yields 24 matches." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
